Web Speech recognition on OHOS uses the system recognizer, through the shell.

On desktop builds SpeechRecognition sends audio to Google's speech service,
which needs an API key this build does not have, so recognition failed with
a network error. As on Android, recognition and audio capture are left to
the system: SpeechRecognizerImplOhos (here, so no new source file) asks a
handler chrome registers (content/public/browser/ohos_speech_recognizer.h,
in the overlay) to start, stop and abort, and turns what the shell reports
back into the listener's events on the IO thread.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-speech-recognition.patch

